{
  "title": "iOS UI tests: kAXErrorIPCTimeout waiting for the login screen of a fresh launch",
  "description": "PR #729 run 37082683506 attempt 2: testTextRecipeReviewAndSave stalled 36 s waiting for the app to idle on the login screen of a fresh launch, then failed with 'Failed to get list of active applications: Accessibility error kAXErrorIPCTimeout'. \
This happens before login, so the recipe-cache sync (moved off the main thread in the PR that fixed the post-login main-thread stall) cannot cause it. \
It looks like a degraded CI simulator rather than the app, but that is unconfirmed. \
To diagnose: download the failed run's ios-ui-test-results artifact. \
The xcresult Data/ blobs are zstd-compressed; one holds the app's console log. \
Check whether the app logged XCTPerformOnMainRunLoop 'main thread busy' messages before the timeout (app at fault) or nothing at all (simulator/testmanagerd at fault). \
If it is the simulator, consider rebooting or erasing the simulator before the UI test step, or retrying the launch once.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "flaky-test",
  ],
